# What the image is (D-249). The BioKids packages and the assistant's runtime are
# not in Debian's archive yet: `make` copies them into config/packages.chroot,
# from which live-build installs them like any other package.

# The desktop a parent uses, as a normal Debian Xfce install has it - but
# without Firefox, which the image's hook removes (D-237): the parent's
# browser is Chromium.
task-xfce-desktop
task-laptop
task-turkish
task-english
network-manager-gnome
lightdm-gtk-greeter
chromium-l10n
# Finds Windows, so the boot menu offers it next to BioKids (dual boot).
os-prober
# The kite while the computer starts (D-251).
plymouth
plymouth-themes

# BioKids, the child's desktop and its apps (biokids-desktop recommends them).
biokids-desktop
# The assistant (off until a parent turns it on; the models are downloaded
# from the panel, never shipped) and what it runs on.
biokids-ai
llama.cpp-tools
whisper.cpp-tools
kiwix-tools
